    "\n",
    "## Overview\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook walks through a traditional NLP pipeline for classifying customer\n",
    "complaint text into product categories. We will go from raw text in a SQLite\n",
    "database all the way to a trained classifier, explaining each step along the way.\n",
    "\n",
    "The general workflow is:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Load the data from SQLite\n",
    "2. Clean and preprocess the text\n",
    "3. Convert text to numbers (TF-IDF vectorization)\n",
    "4. Train a classifier (Logistic Regression)\n",
    "5. Evaluate how well it performs\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. Connect to the Database\n",
    "\n",
    "The complaint data lives in a SQLite file at `data/complaints.db`. SQLite is a\n",
    "lightweight database that is stored as a single file — no server required. Python's\n",
    "built-in `sqlite3` module can connect to it directly. We use `pandas` to read the\n",
    "query result into a DataFrame so the rest of the workflow can treat the data like a\n",
    "table."
   ]
