   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 4. TF-IDF Vectorization\n",
    "\n",
    "Machine learning models cannot work with raw strings — they need numbers. TF-IDF\n",
    "(Term Frequency–Inverse Document Frequency) is the classic way to convert text\n",
    "into a numeric matrix.\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Term Frequency (TF)**: how often a word appears in one document.\n",
    "- **Inverse Document Frequency (IDF)**: penalizes words that appear in almost every\n",
    "  document (they are not useful for distinguishing categories).\n",
    "\n",
    "The result is a matrix where each row is a complaint and each column is a word.\n",
    "The value in a cell represents how important that word is to that specific complaint\n",
    "relative to all others.\n",
    "\n",
    "`max_features=3000` caps the vocabulary at the 3,000 most useful words to keep\n",
    "the matrix manageable. `ngram_range=(1, 2)` means we also capture two-word phrases\n",
    "(bigrams) like \"late fee\" or \"interest rate\", which often carry more meaning than\n",
    "individual words alone."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "446fcad5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Feature matrix shape: (500, 1802)\n",
      "  500 complaints x 1802 TF-IDF features\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import TfidfVectorizer\n",
    "\n",
    "vectorizer = TfidfVectorizer(max_features=3000, ngram_range=(1, 2))\n",
    "\n",
    "# fit_transform does two things at once:\n",
    "#   fit   — learns the vocabulary from the text\n",
    "#   transform — converts the text into the TF-IDF matrix\n",
    "X = vectorizer.fit_transform(df[\"clean_text\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Our target (what we want to predict) is the product category.\n",
    "y = df[\"product_category\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Feature matrix shape: {X.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  {X.shape[0]} complaints x {X.shape[1]} TF-IDF features\")"
   ]
  },
