    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 6. Train a Logistic Regression Classifier\n",
    "\n",
    "Logistic Regression is a simple but surprisingly effective classifier for text.\n",
    "It learns a weight for each TF-IDF feature that indicates how much that word\n",
    "pushes a document toward (or away from) each category.\n",
    "\n",
    "We use it here rather than a more complex model (like a neural network) because:\n",
    "\n",
    "- It trains fast even on a small dataset.\n",
    "- The learned weights are interpretable — we can see which words drive each category.\n",
    "- It tends to work well when TF-IDF features are already informative.\n",
    "\n",
    "`max_iter=1000` gives the optimizer enough iterations to converge.\n",
    "`C=1.0` is the regularization strength — higher values fit the training data more\n",
    "tightly, lower values produce a smoother model that generalizes better."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "bca8c16b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
