    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 7. Evaluate the Classifier\n",
    "\n",
    "Now we measure how well the model performs on the held-out test set. The\n",
    "classification report shows:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Precision** — of all the times the model predicted a category, how often was it right?\n",
    "- **Recall** — of all the actual examples of a category, how many did the model find?\n",
    "- **F1-score** — the harmonic mean of precision and recall; a single number that\n",
    "  balances both. Closer to 1.0 is better.\n",
    "- **Support** — how many real examples of that category were in the test set.\n",
    "\n",
    "Low scores on a category usually mean either (a) too few training examples or\n",
    "(b) that category's language overlaps heavily with another."
   ]
