    "  to get higher precision at the cost of lower coverage, or move left to label\n",
    "  more complaints automatically at the cost of accepting more labeling errors.\n",
    "  A good operating threshold is where the precision line reaches an acceptable\n",
    "  level while the shaded coverage region is still large enough to be useful.\n",
    "  A category whose precision line is already high at low thresholds (flat and\n",
    "  near 1.0 across the chart) needs little or no tuning. A category with a steep\n",
    "  rising curve has more room to improve precision by raising the threshold.\n",
